{title: Filled With Righteousness}
{subtitle: Matthew 5:6}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm7] |
| [Ab] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Poor in spirit, the kin[Bb/D]gdom is yours
[Cm7]Mourning hearts will find com[Ab]fort in store
[Eb]Meek in spirit, the earth [Bb/D]is the prize
[Cm7]Hunger and thirst, with o[Ab]pen wide eyes
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Blessed are [Eb]those who hunger and [Bb]thirst for righteous[Cm7]ness
For they will be [Ab]filled
Blessed are [Eb]those who hunger and [Bb]thirst for righteous[Cm7]ness
For they will be [Ab]filled
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Merciful spirits, [Bb/D]mercy will flow
[Cm7]Pure in heart, you will see [Ab]God’s glow
Peace[Eb]makers rise, [Bb/D]called God’s own sons
The [Cm7]beatitudes speak, the [Ab]victory won
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Fm7]Not by our own [Bb]strength, but by [Cm7]grace
[Fm7]The hunger is [Bb]met in a holy [Eb]place
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Blessed are those who hunger and [Bb]thirst for righteous[Cm7]ness
For they will be [Ab]filled
Blessed are [Eb]those who hunger and [Bb]thirst for righteous[Cm7]ness
For they will be [Ab]filled
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]Filled with the [Bb/D]promise, [Cm7]filled with the [Ab]light
[Eb]Hungering for [Bb/D]what is [Cm7]right [Ab]
{end_of_verse}
